Ivanti's own description of CVE-2026-104935, as the numbering authority, reads "Authentication bypass by spoofing in ICS before version 25.1.3.0 allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary commands" ([ENISA EUVD, 2026-10-13](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-98816)). Rapid7 relays that, according to Ivanti, a portion of the flaw was found through its product security program and patched in the July 2026 release of 25.1.3.0, and that exploitation occurred while Ivanti was backporting the fix to the other supported versions ([Rapid7, 2026-10-13](https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/etr-ivanti-connect-secure-zero-day-exploited-in-the-wild-cve-2026-104935/)). CERT-FR still lists 25.1.3.x builds before 25.1.3.1 as affected ([CERT-FR, 2026-10-14](https://www.cert.ssi.gouv.fr/alerte/CERTFR-2026-ALE-013/)), so 25.1.3.1 remains the build to reach on that line.
